---
import { LENSES } from '../lib/lenses';
---

<section class="lens-picker" data-lens-picker aria-labelledby="lens-heading">
  <p class="mono-label">How should this read</p>
  <h2 id="lens-heading" class="section__title">Same lessons, three doors</h2>
  <p class="section__lede">
    Pick the background closest to yours. The facts stay the same. The opening, the example, and the
    task change. Switch anytime — a link can carry the door you picked.
  </p>
  <div class="lens-choices" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="lens-heading">
    {
      LENSES.map((lens) => (
        <label class="lens-choice">
          <input type="radio" name="lens" value={lens.id} data-lens-choice={lens.id} />
          <span class="lens-choice__title">{lens.label}</span>
          <span class="lens-choice__blurb">{lens.blurb}</span>
        </label>
      ))
    }
  </div>
  <p class="lens-picker__pilots">
    Every Foundations and Build lesson has a tailored frame for New to AI, IT, and customers —
    told through Ash’s meetup story. Switch anytime.
    Every lesson is also marked Start here, Useful, or Skim for the door you picked.
  </p>
</section>
